      <h3>Real-World Use Cases</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cybersecurity teams</strong> use OSINT to map their own attack surface — finding exposed servers,
          leaked credentials, or misconfigured services before attackers do.</li>
        <li><strong>Law enforcement</strong> uses OSINT to track suspects, verify alibis, and gather evidence from
          social media and public records.</li>
        <li><strong>Journalists</strong> use OSINT to verify sources, identify war crimes (like the Bellingcat
          investigations into the MH17 shootdown), and investigate corruption.</li>
        <li><strong>Penetration testers</strong> use OSINT in the reconnaissance phase before a simulated attack —
          understanding the target's infrastructure without touching it.</li>
        <li><strong>HR departments</strong> may perform OSINT background checks on candidates' public digital presence.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Fraud investigators</strong> use OSINT to trace fraudulent identities, fake companies, and money
          trails.</li>
      </ul>
