    <!-- TOOL 6: METAGOOFIL -->
    <section id="s10">
      <h2>10. Tool #6 — Metagoofil</h2>
      <div class="tool-card" data-num="06">
        <div class="tool-name">Metagoofil</div>
        <div class="tool-tagline">Document Metadata Extraction Tool</div>
        <p>Metagoofil is a specialized OSINT tool for extracting <strong>metadata from publicly available
            documents</strong>. It uses Google to search for documents (PDFs, Word docs, Excel sheets, PowerPoint files)
          associated with a target domain, downloads them, and then extracts their hidden metadata.</p>
        <h4>What Is Document Metadata?</h4>
        <p>Every document you create carries hidden data beyond its visible content. This <em>metadata</em> can include:
          the <strong>author's name and username</strong>, the software and version used (e.g., "Microsoft Word 16.0"),
          the <strong>computer's hostname</strong>, internal network paths (e.g.,
          <code>\\fileserver01\HR\salaries_2023.xlsx</code>), <strong>GPS coordinates</strong> (for images), creation
          and modification dates, and email addresses.</p>
        <h4>Why This Matters for Reconnaissance</h4>
        <p>A company might publish a financial report as a PDF. Metagoofil extracts the metadata and reveals the
          author's Windows username (<code>john.smith</code>), the internal server path where the file was saved, and
          the exact version of Microsoft Office — all useful for a penetration tester mapping the target's internal
          infrastructure without ever touching their network.</p>
        <h4>Command Example</h4>
        <p><code>metagoofil -d example.com -t pdf,doc,xls -l 100 -o output/</code></p>
        <p>This downloads up to 100 PDF, DOC, and XLS files from <code>example.com</code> and saves extracted metadata
          to the output folder.</p>
        <div class="tool-tags">
          <span class="tag">Metadata</span>
          <span class="tag">Document OSINT</span>
