    <!-- TOOL 8: INTELLIGENCE X -->
    <section id="s12">
      <h2>12. Tool #8 — Intelligence X (IntelX)</h2>
      <div class="tool-card" data-num="08">
        <div class="tool-name">Intelligence X</div>
        <div class="tool-tagline">Search Engine for Leaked &amp; Historical Data</div>
        <p>Intelligence X (IntelX) is a unique OSINT search engine that searches and archives <strong>data from dark web
            sources, data leaks, paste sites, and historical web archives</strong>. It is built for investigators who
          need to find information that is no longer publicly visible on the regular web — deleted posts, leaked
          databases, and archived dark web content.</p>
        <h4>What Makes IntelX Different</h4>
        <p>Unlike Google or Shodan, IntelX indexes content that has been deliberately removed or is only available on
          the dark web. It archives: leaked credential dumps, Tor hidden service content, Telegram channel data, email
          address leaks, Bitcoin blockchain transaction metadata, and much more.</p>
        <h4>Practical Use Cases</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Breach investigation</strong>: Search for your domain and see if any credentials appear in known
            data leaks.</li>
          <li><strong>Persona tracking</strong>: Search a username or email to find historical mentions across platforms
            even after deletion.</li>
          <li><strong>Malware analysis</strong>: Find past samples, C2 servers, and threat actor communications archived
            from dark web forums.</li>
          <li><strong>Journalism</strong>: Archive and search content from sanctioned or censored sources (used with
            appropriate ethical care).</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tool-tags">
          <span class="tag">Dark Web</span>
